=== day
n: 10
title: How real apps are built
subtitle: A taste of React and of servers
hours: 3 hours
page: index.html
slot: app | jsx | App.jsx
slot: server | js | server.js
refs: @page, style.css

--- intro
This morning the teacher showed you a real **React** project and a real **Express** server running on his laptop. This afternoon you try both ideas yourself, in small steps.

In a real project this code lives in files on your computer (React) or on a server (Express), and you'd install tools first: Node.js, and then React or Express with `npm`. The Lab lets you try the ideas without that.

- **Part 1, steps 1 to 6: React.** You rebuild the ShowShelf grid out of **components**: a card, a list of cards, a My List button and a search box.
- **Part 2, steps 7 to 12: a server.** You write the **routes** of a small My List server with Express. A ready-made page talks to it with `fetch`, so you see your server working straight away.

Today is a taste. The goal isn't to master React or Express in one afternoon, but to recognise the ideas when you meet them again. Everything you already know (functions, objects, arrays, `filter`, `fetch`) is used in both.

