Put the new `useState` and the `useEffect` at the top of `App`, under the search state. Inside `load`, the last line is `setTvShows(data.map(toShow));`. Then change `shows.filter(` to `tvShows.filter(`.
--- hint
```jsx
  const [tvShows, setTvShows] = React.useState([]);

  React.useEffect(() => {
    async function load() {
      const response = await fetch("https://api.tvmaze.com/shows?page=0");
      const data = await response.json();
      setTvShows(data.map(toShow));
    }
    load();
  }, []);

  const found = tvShows.filter((show) => ...);
```
